{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bounded Context.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bounded Context.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bounded context bounded context","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bounded Context.md","fileName":"Bounded Context.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bounded Context","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Bounded Context and Organizational Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Bounded Context and Organizational Design","Domain Model","Ubiquitous Language","Bounded Context Ownership","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bounded Context.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bounded Context.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bounded context bounded context","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bounded Context.md","fileName":"Bounded Context.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bounded Context","heading":"Bounded Context","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A bounded context is the explicit boundary within which one [[Domain Model]] and [[Ubiquitous Language]] are internally consistent. The same word can represent different concepts in other contexts without forcing one object to contain every possible meaning. Inside the boundary, code, tests, data, and conversation share the model; across it, relationships and translations must be deliberate. Clear [[Bounded Context Ownership]] gives a team autonomy to change the model without continuous coordination over its internals.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Bounded Context and Organizational Design","Domain Model","Ubiquitous Language","Bounded Context Ownership","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bounded Context.m